('127.737.d.4.F',3,'The basic architecture of most computer systems includes input, processing, output and:','["decoration", "cooling fans only", "storage", "paper"]'::jsonb,2,'IPOS covers input, processing, output, storage.','original'),
('127.737.d.4.F',4,'In the von Neumann architecture, programs and data are both stored in:','["a monitor", "different planets", "a printer", "the same memory"]'::jsonb,3,'Stored-program concept.','original'),
('127.737.d.4.G',3,'The central processing unit performs calculations, while storage devices:','["keep data when the computer is off", "calculate faster", "cool the case", "print"]'::jsonb,0,'Storage holds data persistently.','original'),
('127.737.d.4.G',4,'A peripheral device such as a printer connects to the computer to:','["cool the CPU", "provide input or output beyond the core system", "replace the CPU", "store the OS"]'::jsonb,1,'Peripherals extend functions.','original'),
('127.737.d.4.H',3,'Servers are kept in rooms with controlled temperature and humidity because:','["it looks nice", "it saves paper", "heat and moisture can damage equipment", "it speeds the mouse"]'::jsonb,2,'Environmental control protects hardware.','original'),
('127.737.d.4.H',4,'A device used to control the temperature of a server room is a:','["stapler", "lamp", "calculator", "thermostat-controlled air conditioner"]'::jsonb,3,'HVAC controls the environment.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.A',3,'Before using a drill to mount a rack, a technician should:','["wear eye protection and secure the work", "remove safety gear", "skip instructions", "use bare hands"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe tool use protects the user.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.A',4,'Safe use of hand tools in computer repair includes:','["using a damaged tool", "using the right size screwdriver and keeping tools in good condition", "using a hammer for every task", "leaving tools on the floor"]'::jsonb,1,'Proper tool use prevents injury and damage.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.B',3,'A technician stuck on an error searches the manufacturer''s support site and a manual. This is:','["avoiding information", "ignoring the problem", "using reference tools and Internet sources for information", "guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'References solve problems.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.B',4,'The most reliable source for a printer''s error code meaning is:','["a rumor", "a guess", "an anonymous post", "the manufacturer''s official documentation"]'::jsonb,3,'Official docs are most reliable.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.C',3,'Old batteries and monitors with hazardous materials should be:','["taken to a certified recycling or disposal program", "buried", "thrown in regular trash", "burned"]'::jsonb,0,'Hazardous materials need proper disposal.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.C',4,'Disposing of electronic equipment with lead and mercury properly protects:','["only the printer", "the environment and people''s health", "only the owner''s wallet", "no one"]'::jsonb,1,'Proper disposal prevents contamination.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.D',3,'A new technology that uses qubits to perform certain calculations is called:','["manual computing", "paper computing", "quantum computing", "analog computing"]'::jsonb,2,'Quantum computers use quantum bits.','original'),
('127.737.d.5.D',4,'Emerging technologies like quantum computing and artificial intelligence may affect computer technology careers by:','["removing electricity", "ending all careers", "making no change", "changing the skills employers need"]'::jsonb,3,'New tech shifts job needs.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.A',3,'A student notices that a lab''s PCs freeze every Friday afternoon. Naming this issue is:','["identifying a problem relating to IT", "solving the problem", "avoiding it", "publishing a solution"]'::jsonb,0,'Naming starts problem solving.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.A',4,'A clear IT problem statement should be:','["already solved", "specific enough to guide research and testing", "so broad it can''t be tested", "unrelated"]'::jsonb,1,'Specific statements focus work.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.B',3,'To fix repeated PC freezes, a student plans an update using appropriate technologies and IT standards. This is:','["guessing", "copying", "developing a solution that follows technology standards", "ignoring standards"]'::jsonb,2,'Solutions use standards.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.B',4,'When developing a solution, using IT industry standards helps ensure the solution:','["is untested", "is unique but incompatible", "is hidden", "works with other systems and meets accepted practice"]'::jsonb,3,'Standards promote compatibility.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.C',3,'A student tells the class that replacing the failing RAM will end the freezing and describes how they will test it. This is:','["explaining how the solution resolves the problem and the methods used", "guessing", "avoiding testing", "hiding the plan"]'::jsonb,0,'Explanations link solution and method.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.C',4,'A good explanation of a proposed solution includes the:','["logo", "methodology that will confirm the problem is fixed", "colors", "slogans"]'::jsonb,1,'Methods prove the fix.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.D',3,'Choosing between replacing RAM and reinstalling the OS by comparing cost, time and risk is a:','["guess", "avoidance", "decision-making technique", "coin flip"]'::jsonb,2,'Comparing criteria supports decisions.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.D',4,'Applying a decision-making technique to pick a technology solution means:','["choosing the cheapest only", "avoiding options", "choosing randomly", "weighing options against stated criteria"]'::jsonb,3,'Criteria drive decisions.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.E',3,'Choosing ECC memory for a server helps design in:','["reliability", "noise", "clutter", "delays"]'::jsonb,0,'Error-correcting memory reduces failures.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.E',4,'Which choice builds safety into a computer lab design?','["loose cables", "grounded outlets and cable covers", "blocked exits", "overloaded power strips"]'::jsonb,1,'Safe layouts reduce hazards.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.F',3,'A student questions assumptions, tests the fix and checks the data before accepting it. This is:','["copying", "avoiding checks", "critical-thinking analysis and evaluation of a solution", "accepting without proof"]'::jsonb,2,'Evaluation uses evidence.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.F',4,'Evaluating a proposed technological solution critically means asking:','["is it popular?", "is it expensive?", "is it colorful?", "does the evidence show it works and what could go wrong?"]'::jsonb,3,'Critical evaluation looks at evidence and risk.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.G',3,'A sustainability plan for a computer lab fix describes how the solution will be:','["maintained and supported over time", "abandoned", "forgotten", "hidden"]'::jsonb,0,'Sustainability keeps solutions working.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.G',4,'Part of a sustainability plan for a replacement PC program is:','["avoiding budgets", "scheduling updates and replacement cycles", "ignoring updates", "removing support"]'::jsonb,1,'Planning replacements sustains service.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.H',3,'A student uses a simulator, a spreadsheet and a manual to design and test a network change. This is:','["avoiding tools", "one tool only", "selecting and using appropriate technological resources", "random tools"]'::jsonb,2,'Right tools support research and design.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.H',4,'Choosing technological resources for research and design should be based on:','["which is newest", "which is largest", "which is cheapest only", "how well they fit the task"]'::jsonb,3,'Fit to task matters.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.I',3,'Notes, drafts, test logs and diagrams kept throughout a project make up its:','["documentation of the research and development process", "final exam", "budget", "trash"]'::jsonb,0,'Documentation records the process.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.I',4,'Good R&D documentation should be:','["unordered", "dated, organized and detailed enough for others to follow", "hidden", "vague"]'::jsonb,1,'Clear records are useful.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.J',3,'At the end of the project, the student presents the solution to a panel of professionals using:','["reading from notes without looking up", "silence", "formal presentation skills", "casual chat"]'::jsonb,2,'Panels expect polish.','original'),
('127.737.d.6.J',4,'A professional presentation of a solution to a panel includes:','["a hurried exit", "only the title", "only a joke", "a clear problem, the solution, evidence and answers to questions"]'::jsonb,3,'Complete presentations are persuasive.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.A',3,'A project begins with initiating and planning, then executing, monitoring and controlling, and finally closing. These are:','["project methodology phases", "file types", "network cables", "hardware parts"]'::jsonb,0,'Project management follows phases.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.A',4,'In the monitoring and controlling phase, the project manager:','["starts the plan", "tracks progress and makes corrections", "ignores issues", "ends the project"]'::jsonb,1,'Monitoring keeps projects on track.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.B',3,'The scope of work statement for a lab upgrade lists:','["only lunch plans", "only the budget", "what will and won''t be included in the project", "nothing"]'::jsonb,2,'Scope sets boundaries.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.B',4,'Defining scope helps a team avoid:','["all costs", "all risks", "all deadlines", "scope creep, where extra work keeps being added"]'::jsonb,3,'Clear scope controls growth.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.C',3,'A project plan lists each task, who does it and when it is due. This is a:','["time and activity plan", "recipe", "logo", "slogan"]'::jsonb,0,'Activity plans schedule tasks.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.C',4,'Which tool is commonly used to show task schedules over time?','["a pie chart only", "a Gantt chart", "a flowchart only", "a bar code"]'::jsonb,1,'Gantt charts show schedules.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.D',3,'A project team includes a network engineer, a developer and a trainer who each handle their own area. This is a:','["random group", "one-person team", "cross-functional team", "single-skill team"]'::jsonb,2,'Cross-functional teams combine skills.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.D',4,'The advantage of a cross-functional team is that it:','["duplicates work", "avoids communication", "limits skills", "brings different expertise to reach project goals"]'::jsonb,3,'Diverse skills solve complex projects.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.E',3,'A QA test plan lists test cases, expected results and who runs them. This ensures:','["the product meets requirements before release", "deadlines vanish", "it is never tested", "bugs stay hidden"]'::jsonb,0,'Test plans verify quality.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.E',4,'A quality assurance test plan should include:','["only opinions", "test cases, pass/fail criteria and a way to log defects", "only the title", "no steps"]'::jsonb,1,'Good plans are specific.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.F',3,'A contingency plan describes what to do if:','["no one works", "the budget is perfect", "something goes wrong with the project", "everything goes right"]'::jsonb,2,'Contingency plans prepare for problems.','original'),
('127.737.d.7.F',4,'A contingency plan for a server migration should include:','["no contacts", "no backups", "random steps", "a rollback procedure and backup contacts"]'::jsonb,3,'Fallback plans reduce risk.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.A',3,'Viruses, ransomware and phishing are examples of:','["security threats to information systems", "office supplies", "display types", "software upgrades"]'::jsonb,0,'Threats target systems.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.A',4,'A threat that locks files until money is paid is called:','["a driver", "ransomware", "bandwidth", "firmware"]'::jsonb,1,'Ransomware encrypts files for ransom.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.B',3,'A security lapse, such as an unpatched server, can lead to:','["faster networks", "higher grades", "data breaches and loss of trust", "free upgrades"]'::jsonb,2,'Lapses create vulnerabilities.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.B',4,'Identifying security needs means deciding what must be protected, such as:','["only furniture", "only paper", "nothing", "customer data, system access and equipment"]'::jsonb,3,'Assets drive security needs.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.C',3,'After finding that employees reuse weak passwords, a team writes a plan with password rules and training. This is:','["developing and implementing a plan to address a threat", "deleting accounts", "ignoring the threat", "blaming users"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans address identified risks.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.C',4,'An effective security plan includes controls, responsibilities and:','["no owners", "a way to monitor whether the controls work", "no review", "no monitoring"]'::jsonb,1,'Monitoring verifies controls.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.D',3,'Writing down the steps for revoking a departed employee''s access is:','["deleting steps", "wasting time", "documenting security procedures", "hiding information"]'::jsonb,2,'Documented procedures ensure consistency.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.D',4,'Documented security procedures help organizations because they:','["slow everything", "remove accountability", "hide mistakes", "make responses consistent and auditable"]'::jsonb,3,'Procedures create consistency.','original'),
('127.737.d.8.E',3,'Investigators examining a hacked computer to find evidence are using:','["computer forensics", "gardening", "interior design", "cooking"]'::jsonb,0,'Forensics gathers digital evidence.','original')
