('127.737.d.8.E',4,'A key rule in computer forensics is to:','["delete logs", "preserve the original evidence and work from copies", "share evidence publicly", "alter the original"]'::jsonb,1,'Evidence integrity matters.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.A',3,'A technician lets a client explain a problem without interrupting and takes notes. This is:','["guessing", "ignoring the client", "effective listening to identify support needs", "rushing"]'::jsonb,2,'Listening reveals needs.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.A',4,'To confirm understanding of a client''s request, a technician should:','["end the call", "assume correctness", "avoid questions", "restate it in their own words and ask if it''s right"]'::jsonb,3,'Paraphrasing confirms understanding.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.B',3,'After listening, a technician lists the client''s needs and outlines steps and timeframes. This is:','["identifying customer need and formulating a support plan", "canceling service", "guessing", "avoiding work"]'::jsonb,0,'Needs drive support plans.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.B',4,'A support plan should include:','["no owner", "the goal, the steps, the responsible person and the timeline", "no goal", "no steps"]'::jsonb,1,'Plans are actionable.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.C',3,'A technician runs a report of all computers with outdated software and checks system information. This is:','["guessing", "deleting logs", "creating queries and reports to assess system information", "avoiding data"]'::jsonb,2,'Queries and reports reveal conditions.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.C',4,'A query that lists only machines with less than 10% free disk space helps the technician to:','["ignore the machines", "rename the machines", "delete the machines", "find systems that need attention first"]'::jsonb,3,'Targeted queries prioritize work.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.D',3,'A technician uses a step-by-step method to find why a laptop won''t charge and then fixes it. This is:','["problem-solving in support, maintenance and repair", "blaming", "avoiding", "guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'Methodical problem solving fixes issues.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.D',4,'The first step in solving a repair problem is usually to:','["give up", "define the problem and gather information", "replace parts at random", "skip diagnosis"]'::jsonb,1,'Diagnosis precedes repair.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.E',3,'A program that tests memory and a tool that checks hard drive health are examples of:','["fonts", "games", "hardware and software diagnostics", "wallpapers"]'::jsonb,2,'Diagnostics find faults.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.E',4,'Running a diagnostic before replacing a part helps avoid:','["all testing", "all learning", "all support", "unnecessary repairs and costs"]'::jsonb,3,'Diagnose first.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.F',3,'After fixing a problem, the technician tells the user what caused it and what was done. This is:','["reporting the cause and solution to the user", "ignoring the user", "blaming the user", "hiding the cause"]'::jsonb,0,'Users should know the result.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.F',4,'When reporting a solution to a non-technical user, the technician should:','["blame them", "explain in plain language and offer prevention tips", "use heavy jargon", "skip details"]'::jsonb,1,'Clear explanations build trust.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.G',3,'A ticket note lists the symptom, cause and fix so others can use it later. This is:','["a disposable note", "an error", "written documentation of the problem and its solution", "a delay"]'::jsonb,2,'Documentation preserves knowledge.','original'),
('127.737.d.9.G',4,'Documentation of a repair should be:','["vague", "incomplete", "hidden", "clear, accurate and stored where others can find it"]'::jsonb,3,'Findable records help the team.','original'),
('127.737.d.10.A',3,'A technician installs an antivirus program on a new workstation. This is:','["installing security software", "hiding software", "deleting software", "removing protection"]'::jsonb,0,'Security software protects systems.','original'),
('127.737.d.10.A',4,'Before installing security software, a technician should confirm that:','["it is free of any license", "it is from a trusted source and compatible with the system", "it is old", "it is unknown"]'::jsonb,1,'Verify source and compatibility.','original'),
('127.737.d.10.B',3,'Antivirus definitions must be updated regularly so the software can:','["print faster", "use less power", "detect the newest threats", "look better"]'::jsonb,2,'Definitions identify known malware.','original'),
('127.737.d.10.B',4,'Setting security software to update automatically ensures that it:','["needs no testing", "stops working", "blocks all files", "stays current without relying on users"]'::jsonb,3,'Automatic updates keep protection fresh.','original'),
('127.737.d.10.C',3,'A technician boots an infected computer into safe mode and runs a full scan to remove malware. This is:','["using security software to clean an infected machine", "deleting the OS", "spreading the malware", "ignoring the issue"]'::jsonb,0,'Scans remove threats.','original'),
('127.737.d.10.C',4,'After cleaning an infected machine, the technician should:','["assume it''s clean", "re-scan, apply updates and change passwords as needed", "reinstall the malware", "share the infection"]'::jsonb,1,'Verification and hardening finish the job.','original'),
('127.737.d.11.A',3,'A written disaster recovery plan explains how to:','["delete systems", "avoid backups", "restore systems and data after a major failure", "ignore outages"]'::jsonb,2,'DR plans restore operations.','original'),
('127.737.d.11.A',4,'A disaster recovery plan should list:','["random notes", "only passwords", "only lunch menus", "critical systems, backup locations and recovery steps"]'::jsonb,3,'Specifics enable recovery.','original'),
('127.737.d.11.B',3,'A written preventive maintenance plan schedules tasks such as:','["cleaning fans, checking cables and applying updates", "deleting logs", "ignoring equipment", "waiting for failure"]'::jsonb,0,'Preventive maintenance reduces failures.','original'),
('127.737.d.11.B',4,'A preventive maintenance schedule helps an IT department by:','["increasing failures", "reducing unexpected failures and downtime", "ending support", "removing documentation"]'::jsonb,1,'Regular upkeep prevents problems.','original'),
('127.737.d.12.A',3,'A student collects project reports, certifications and volunteer records into a career portfolio. This is:','["deleting work", "hiding work", "documenting projects and accomplishments", "losing work"]'::jsonb,2,'Portfolios show achievements.','original'),
('127.737.d.12.A',4,'A portfolio documents academics, volunteer experience and:','["only recipes", "only pets", "only games", "employment and certifications"]'::jsonb,3,'Breadth shows readiness.','original'),
('127.737.d.12.B',3,'A student places the best, most relevant items at the front of the portfolio. This is:','["organizing and prioritizing information", "hiding it", "scrambling it", "deleting it"]'::jsonb,0,'Prioritizing guides reviewers.','original'),
('127.737.d.12.B',4,'The best way to organize a portfolio for a hiring manager is by:','["random order", "relevance to the job and clear sections", "alphabet only", "file size"]'::jsonb,1,'Relevance and structure help readers.','original'),
('127.737.d.12.C',3,'A portfolio''s cover letter, slide show and oral presentation show:','["no skills", "one skill", "written, verbal and visual communication skills", "only typing"]'::jsonb,2,'Portfolios demonstrate communication.','original'),
('127.737.d.12.C',4,'Communication in a portfolio should be consistent with:','["no rules", "random style", "slang", "IT industry standards for clarity and professionalism"]'::jsonb,3,'Industry standards guide quality.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.A',3,'In an advanced practicum, a student drafts a project memo, gives a verbal update to a client and shares a system diagram. This uses:','["written, verbal and visual communication consistent with IT standards", "only email", "one type of communication", "no communication"]'::jsonb,0,'Practicum communication blends forms.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.A',4,'Which communication practice meets IT industry standards?','["Relying on memory only", "Documenting decisions in a clear, dated written record", "Using unexplained slang", "Skipping written updates"]'::jsonb,1,'Standards favor clear records.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.B',3,'A technician reads log data, summarizes the likely cause and explains it to a manager. This is:','["ignoring data", "hiding information", "analyzing, interpreting and communicating information", "guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'Analysis plus communication drives action.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.B',4,'To effectively communicate technical findings to a non-technical audience, a technician should:','["read raw logs aloud", "avoid questions", "use the most jargon possible", "translate details into plain language and focus on impact"]'::jsonb,3,'Audience-aware communication works best.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.C',3,'A technician pauses, nods and asks a clarifying question when a client describes an error. This is:','["active listening to obtain and clarify information", "ignoring", "interrupting", "multitasking"]'::jsonb,0,'Active listening obtains accurate details.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.C',4,'Which question helps clarify a vague client report like ''the network is down''?','["Did you try turning off the building?", "Which devices or locations are affected and since when?", "Is it Friday?", "Why are you bothering me?"]'::jsonb,1,'Specific questions reduce ambiguity.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.D',3,'A technician follows up after a fix to be sure the client is satisfied. This is:','["avoiding contact", "hiding results", "public relations skills that maintain customer satisfaction", "ignoring the customer"]'::jsonb,2,'Follow-up builds relationships.','original'),
('127.738.d.1.D',4,'Keeping internal clients, such as accounting, satisfied with IT service includes:','["blaming them", "avoiding updates", "delaying replies", "meeting commitments and communicating delays early"]'::jsonb,3,'Reliability and transparency maintain trust.','original'),
('127.738.d.2',3,'A student faces a complex outage, examines possible causes, tests solutions and selects the best fix, working alone and with a team. This reflects:','["advanced problem-solving using critical thinking and decision making", "copying the fix", "random guessing", "avoiding the problem"]'::jsonb,0,'Advanced problem solving combines analysis and decisions.','original'),
('127.738.d.2',4,'A student demonstrating advanced problem-solving with increased fluency will:','["pick the first idea", "evaluate alternatives and justify a technology-based decision", "avoid data", "rely on luck"]'::jsonb,1,'Justified decisions show advanced skill.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.A',3,'A student follows the lab''s rules for passwords, visitor logs and equipment checkout every day. This is:','["ignoring rules", "skipping logs", "understanding and consistently following IT security rules", "sharing logins"]'::jsonb,2,'Consistency is key to security.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.A',4,'Following IT security procedures consistently reduces the risk of:','["faster networks", "higher grades", "free equipment", "breaches caused by human error"]'::jsonb,3,'Procedures limit mistakes.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.B',3,'A technician sees repeated failed logins from an unknown address, blocks it and updates the firewall software. This is:','["recognizing a threat and addressing it with security software", "ignoring the alert", "deleting logs", "sharing the address"]'::jsonb,0,'Detect and respond.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.B',4,'After recognizing a threat, a technician should install updates and:','["ignore logs", "verify the protection is working", "assume it works", "disable it"]'::jsonb,1,'Verification closes the loop.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.C',3,'A student explains that an unpatched server could expose customer records. This is:','["hiding records", "avoiding review", "identifying security needs and the problems lapses cause", "ignoring risk"]'::jsonb,2,'Understanding consequences guides security.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.C',4,'With increased proficiency, a technician can predict which security lapse would cause the greatest harm and:','["avoid planning", "ignore it", "treat all risks the same", "prioritize protections for those systems first"]'::jsonb,3,'Risk-based prioritization.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.D',3,'Before using a power drill to install a rack, a technician should:','["wear safety glasses and check the tool", "use a broken tool", "skip safety", "use bare hands"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe tool use protects people.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.D',4,'With increased proficiency in computer technology safety, a technician will:','["need constant reminders", "use tools correctly without being reminded", "avoid safety", "skip checks"]'::jsonb,1,'Proficiency shows in habits.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.E',3,'Used toner cartridges and batteries are handled as hazardous materials and should be:','["thrown in regular trash", "buried", "disposed of through approved recycling programs", "burned"]'::jsonb,2,'Hazardous materials need proper disposal.','original'),
('127.738.d.3.E',4,'Proper disposal of environmentally hazardous IT materials protects:','["only the budget", "only the building", "no one", "people and the environment from harmful substances"]'::jsonb,3,'Disposal laws protect health.','original'),
('127.738.d.4.A',3,'A student completes assigned tasks on time and with care without being reminded. This shows:','["a positive, productive work ethic", "neglect", "avoidance", "a poor attitude"]'::jsonb,0,'Reliability reflects work ethic.','original'),
('127.738.d.4.A',4,'Performing tasks as directed in a practicum includes:','["avoiding feedback", "following instructions and asking questions when unsure", "guessing", "ignoring instructions"]'::jsonb,1,'Following directions and seeking clarity is professional.','original'),
('127.738.d.4.B',3,'An IT employee refuses to read a coworker''s private email even though they have admin access. This is:','["ignoring ethics", "breaking rules", "practicing ethical responsibilities in IT", "spying"]'::jsonb,2,'Access doesn''t mean permission.','original'),
('127.738.d.4.B',4,'Which is a legal responsibility in the field of IT?','["copying software freely", "ignoring licenses", "selling user data", "complying with software licensing and data protection laws"]'::jsonb,3,'IT workers must follow laws.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_92_v1'
from (values
('127.738.d.4.C',3,'A technician admits to a mistake that caused a short outage rather than hiding it. This shows:','["integrity by choosing the ethical course", "blame shifting", "dishonesty", "avoidance"]'::jsonb,0,'Integrity means honesty.','original'),
('127.738.d.4.C',4,'When a manager asks for a shortcut that violates policy, a person with integrity will:','["break the policy", "explain the policy and follow the rules", "blame a coworker", "hide the issue"]'::jsonb,1,'Ethics outweigh convenience.','original'),
('127.738.d.4.D',3,'A student complies with the school''s acceptable-use policy and copyright law at all times. This is:','["hiding violations", "breaking rules sometimes", "complying with all applicable rules, laws and regulations consistently", "ignoring laws"]'::jsonb,2,'Consistent compliance is professional.','original'),
('127.738.d.4.D',4,'Consistent compliance with regulations in IT matters because noncompliance can result in:','["higher pay", "new equipment", "faster networks", "fines, legal action and loss of trust"]'::jsonb,3,'Noncompliance has consequences.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.A',3,'A student chooses a ticketing system to track tasks, a wiki to document and a spreadsheet to evaluate results. This is:','["selecting and using appropriate technological resources", "random tools", "no tools", "one tool only"]'::jsonb,0,'Right tools support learning activities.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.A',4,'A technological resource should be selected based on whether it:','["is newest", "fits the task and supports documentation and evaluation", "looks best", "is largest"]'::jsonb,1,'Fit to task matters.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.B',3,'A technician reads a rack diagram and wiring schematic to plan a cabling job. This is:','["guessing", "skipping plans", "reading and interpreting technical documentation", "ignoring diagrams"]'::jsonb,2,'Diagrams guide installations.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.B',4,'Which document would best show how network devices are physically connected?','["a calendar", "a menu", "a poster", "a network diagram"]'::jsonb,3,'Diagrams show topology.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.C',3,'A technician uses vendor manuals, forums and search engines fluently to resolve an unfamiliar error. This is:','["employing reference tools and Internet sources with fluency", "avoiding information", "ignoring the error", "guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'Fluent research solves problems.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.C',4,'A technician evaluating information from a forum should:','["apply it blindly", "verify it against official documentation before applying it", "ignore all sources", "trust it automatically"]'::jsonb,1,'Verify unverified advice.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.D',3,'A student designs a backup strategy using industry-standard practices and appropriate tools. This is:','["guessing", "copying", "developing a solution using technologies, IT concepts and standards", "avoiding standards"]'::jsonb,2,'Solutions follow standards.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.D',4,'Developing solutions with increased proficiency means the student can:','["need constant help", "ignore standards", "avoid testing", "design, test and justify solutions that meet standards"]'::jsonb,3,'Proficiency shows independence.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.E',3,'A student uses scope, schedule and quality checkpoints to manage an information system upgrade. This is:','["implementing project methodologies to manage projects", "working randomly", "skipping steps", "avoiding planning"]'::jsonb,0,'Methodologies guide projects.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.E',4,'A project methodology for an information system project typically moves from planning to:','["random work", "execution, monitoring and closing", "deletion", "confusion"]'::jsonb,1,'Phases structure the project.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.F',3,'A student saves a finished design document, a test report and a client letter as proof of their practicum work. These are:','["drafts only", "blank pages", "representative work samples", "unrelated files"]'::jsonb,2,'Samples demonstrate skills.','original'),
('127.738.d.5.F',4,'Representative work samples should be:','["unfinished", "unlabeled", "random", "relevant, high quality and clearly labeled"]'::jsonb,3,'Good samples are curated.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
